For every load-bearing manuscript claim $c$ whose component kinds lie in the seven-kind domain, $V(c, C)$ is a finite, prose-insensitive record-schema verifier for the declared publication certificate. If $V$ accepts, then $ C(c)$ is locally checkable at exactly its declared evidence level. This is certificate-record verification only: it checks finite record shape, dispatch, evidence pointers, and command-boundary discipline, not end-to-end external semantic validation of the referenced artifacts or source theory. If $V$ rejects, then a reviewer can extract a finite bad subrecord consisting of the first failed schema check and the fields on which that check depends.

