1464-1469 proposition prop:gate-interface-separation [Gate-interface separation]
The promotion, overlap, submission-state, and theorem-content delta gates are separate deterministic interfaces. None can be replaced by passage of another one when a load-bearing claim has the corresponding component.

1488-1501 proposition prop:scheduler-selection-advisory [Scheduler selection is advisory before discovery gating]
Let $s$ be a scheduler or critical-path score attached to a candidate claim $c$. If $s$ recommends selecting $c$, then the recommendation is a work-selection claim and by itself can only pass the scheduler gate. If $c$ is also asserted to be a discovery or classifier-shifting contribution in a record-gate-sound pipeline, then the accepted mixed claim must pass both the scheduler gate and the discovery gate. Consequently, critical-path scores may prioritize review order, and the imported classifier-shift selection rule may break ties among otherwise equal discovery potential coordinates, but neither score nor recommendation accepts a classifier-shift discovery unless the discovery gate also supplies the required certificate, ledger, and lineage witnesses.

