1707-1724 proposition prop:publication-safety-maximality [Finite-record maximality]
Under the hypotheses of Theorem~thm:publication-safety-interface, the constructed certificate is maximal with respect to the finite submitted record surface. More precisely, let $c$ be an accepted load-bearing claim and let $Cert_{}(c)=(K,,E,H,R,D,B)$ be the certificate constructed in that theorem. If a stronger reading $c^{+}$ asserts any external end-to-end compiler correctness, current execution of unrecorded gates, proof-assistant correctness, current formal-source currency, dynamic artifact semantics, or venue acceptance, then either $c^{+}$ is not a distinct finite-record consequence of $Cert_{}(c)$, or its certificate must strictly enlarge one of $K,,E,H,R,D,B$ by adding the corresponding claim kind, evidence surface, gate pass record, promotion or venue field, discovery-interface row, or command-run tuple. In the latter case, if the enlargement is absent, a finite bad subrecord is returned by Theorem~thm:record-acceptance-exactness or by one of the obstruction types of Theorem~thm:finite-certificate-obstruction-skeleton.

