2261-2268 lemma lem:gate-witness-criterion [Gate-witness criterion]
A case record is a path-verified witness for the safety interface when it names the source or artifact surface, the invariant that failed, the gate decision, and the safe manuscript lesson. Under the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~thm:publication-safety-interface, such a witness can support a case-study claim, but not a stronger command-run claim, unless the corresponding command log is also recorded.

2280-2303 proposition prop:path-complete-case-witnesses [Path-complete case witnesses]
Suppose a case-study row is used as load-bearing evidence for the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~thm:publication-safety-interface. If the row is path-complete in the sense above, then the row supplies exactly the evidence surface required for a path-verified historical case claim and no evidence surface for a fresh daemon, full-source, theorem-content, artifact-suite, or semantic-substrate rerun. In fact every accepted path-complete case row factors through one of four finite witness skeletons---promotion, route/submission blocking, theorem-content non-growth, or artifact-limitation disclosure---and its admissible manuscript lesson is the unique bounded lesson attached to that skeleton. Replacing that lesson by a fresh experiment, dynamic validation, or semantic artifact claim changes the skeleton by adding a command-run or artifact-semantic coordinate, so the original row no longer certifies the stronger claim. In particular, a promotion row is sufficient only for the bounded claim that an intake packet is not daemon-visible publication work before human promotion; a route-overlap row is sufficient only for the bounded claim that the overlap and submission-state gates bl ...

2406-2424 proposition prop:review-bundle-case-snapshot-coverage [Review-bundle case-snapshot coverage]
For the four case-study rows in Table~tab:case-witnesses, the review bundle contains a finite external-review surface for every local case path used by the paper. The Newmath block has two local paths, the upper-fibers block has five local paths, the fake-extension block has two local paths, and the Rule110 block has four local paths, for thirteen local-path strings after resolving this paper's relative ARTIFACT_INVENTORY.md to its absolute path in the paper directory. The manifest file review_bundle/REVIEW_BUNDLE_MANIFEST.json has one case_evidence entry for each case row and, inside each entry, a reviewable_snapshots list matching those local paths. File-valued local surfaces are copied into review_bundle/case_snapshots/; directory-valued local surfaces are represented there by directory file-manifests. Consequently the case-study claim made by this paper is externally reviewable at the path-verified snapshot level. It is not a command-run validation claim, a fresh full-source rebuild claim, a daemon-execution claim, or a fresh Rule110 dynamic rerun claim.

2532-2551 proposition audit:fresh-venue-record-criterion [Fresh venue-record criterion]
Assume that the final submitted support surface contains either the venue-check record VENUE_CHECK.md and log VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log, the later local-date rerun log review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-05.log, or an archive-equivalent replacement naming the same checked URLs, observation time, route rules, command result, source state, environment, exit code, and log path. Then the venue row of Proposition~audit:venue-submission-pack-gate is accepted for the current package only when the upload is made on that checked rule state or after a later record with the same fields has replaced it. If that support surface is not submitted, or if an upload occurs after a venue-page change without a replacement record, the package retains only a dated local readiness observation and cannot certify upload-time venue compliance. If the local venue-check files are not part of the submitted support surface, mentions of VENUE_CHECK.md, VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log, and review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-05.log in this supplement are historical/path-verified diagnostic context only, not finite package coordinates for a venue certificate.

2573-2587 theorem thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation [Venue-rule freshness non-escalation]
Let $U$ be the finite dated venue record consisting of the official call URL, the submission-form URL, the style-guideline URL, the observation date and time, the HTTP-status run witness VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log or the later rerun witness review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-05.log, the observed route class, page limit, proceedings boundary, deadline, supplement access rule, and the local witness rows in Table~tab:venue-submission-pack-gate. The venue component of the current finite-record package is accepted exactly for uploads whose venue-rule state is represented by $U$ or by a later replacement record with the same fields. If an upload is made after a venue-page change, or if no upload-time replacement record is supplied, then the package retains only a historical venue observation and cannot certify submission-pack readiness, EasyChair compliance, acceptance, or proceedings status.

2615-2628 corollary cor:historical-venue-record-non-escalation [Historical venue record non-escalation]
The venue check recorded at VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log, with local observation time 2026-06-04 10:15 Asia/Singapore, is a historical venue record. For the present post-2026-06-04 source state it is superseded, for local readiness only, by the rerun log review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-05.log, whose local observation time is 2026-06-05 12:19 Asia/Singapore and whose exit code is 0. Neither dated record certifies actual upload-time EasyChair compliance, acceptance, or proceedings status unless the final submitted support surface also contains either an upload-time record with the same fields or an explicit statement that the upload used the unchanged venue-rule state represented by the latest dated record.

2644-2664 corollary cor:upload-time-venue-compliance-record-requirement [Upload-time venue-compliance record requirement]
The logs VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log and review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-05.log are dated local-readiness records. For the current package they certify only the venue rule state observed at their recorded observation times. They do not certify upload-time EasyChair compliance unless the final submitted support surface also contains either enumerate a later upload-time venue/bibliography record with the same URL, observation-time, command-result, source-state, environment, exit-code, and log-path fields; or a finite statement that the completed upload used the unchanged venue-rule state represented by the latest included dated record. enumerate If neither record is present, all venue-dependent conclusions in Proposition~audit:venue-submission-pack-gate and Table~tab:venue-submission-pack-gate remain historical local-readiness claims and cannot be escalated to upload-time compliance, acceptance, or proceedings-status claims.

