For the current presentation package, every accepted use of a bundle-backed certificate coordinate is in exactly one of the following normal forms. enumerate Exact inclusion: an external upload or submission receipt records that the submitted support surface contains the exact review_bundle/ directory whose certificate-file bytes match review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md. Archive-equivalent inclusion: a replacement archive satisfies every row of Table~tab:review-bundle-archive-equivalence, including manifest identity, bundle-version identity, finite file-list identity, SHA-256 content identity, and relative path semantics. Promoted rerun: the package is advanced to a new source state by rerunning the verifier commands and replacing the displayed source-state record, verifier logs, and digest manifest by one common finite commit--manifest certificate. enumerate If none of these three normal forms is present, the attempted bundle-backed reading has a finite obstruction subrecord: either the external exact-inclusion receipt is absent, the archive-equivalence table has a failed row, or the rerun branch lacks the command, source-state, environment, exit-code, log-path, and digest coor ...

